NAME
    menu-ext-adv - interactive terminal menu with configurable action keys

SYNOPSIS
    menu-ext-adv [-H <header>] [-F <footer>] [-B <bottom-footer>]
                 -K <key> [-K <key> ...] -- <item> ...

DESCRIPTION
    menu-ext-adv renders its UI on /dev/tty and reserves standard output for
    the result.

    Items use:
        <text>
        <value>@:=<text>

    At least one -K action key is required. Pressing a configured action key
    returns:
        <key>@:=<selected-value>

    Escape cancels. Arrow Up/Down, PageUp/PageDown, Home and End are reserved
    navigation keys.

    Configurable keys include one printable ASCII character, space, tab, enter,
    backspace, delete, insert, arrow_left, arrow_right and f1 through f20.

OPTIONS
    -H <header>         Header at the top of the terminal.
    -F <footer>         Footer after the last visible item.
    -B <bottom-footer>  Footer anchored at the bottom.
    -K <key>            Configure an action key; may be repeated.
    -h                  Write command usage.

EXIT STATUS
    0   A configured action key selected the current item.
    1   The menu was cancelled.
    2   Invalid invocation or terminal/setup failure.
